            <ArticleTitle>[Emergencies in general practice, 1. Headache as an alarm symptom].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>28-33</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary headache, such as migraine and tension type headache is a common symptom in patients presenting in emergency departments. Suspicious of secondary headache is a medical history of new onset, changing character of a previously known headache, resistancy to medication or symptoms which are not typical of primary headache.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
